From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:18:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] CR-UI: docs: the footer colour order bug and how it was
 found

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63cvvRYHgPW3b8GJby1n
---
 docs/CREATOR.md | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/CREATOR.md b/docs/CREATOR.md
index e5640db5..3325b126 100644
--- a/docs/CREATOR.md
+++ b/docs/CREATOR.md
@@ -1077,6 +1077,10 @@ grid footer only; the panels, tabs, pane and pickers are as before):
 * **A long value is cut hard on the row.** The selected row is cut with ".." and stands still, so a long name (a long part
   or colour name on a narrow column) can leave only a few letters on the row. This is accepted: the footer line shows the whole
   name, and the test keeps that true for every choice.
+* **The footer's colour is read after the text.** `draw_footer` gets the line and its colour from one call; the colour is
+  read after that call, never in the same argument list (the native runner drew the line black, the Dreamcast build did
+  not: found by the Dreamcast `ui-compare`). `cr_ui_footer_is_drawn_in_the_text_colour` checks the drawn pixels (note: it
+  passes on the test build even with the order bug, which only showed in the runner build; the `ui-compare` is the proof).
 * **Fewer captions.** No caption repeats the tab's name: the Hair tab lost "Hair" (one more row on the GBA), the Voice tab's
   second caption is "Tuning", the Body tab's is "Shape" (the title reads "Body > Shape").
 * **The sliders page says the cheat.** A build slider's line shows "Short <-> Tall  x3" while Slider range is above x1.
